1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born in San Juan on 1 April 1803, she was the eldest sister of D.F. Sarmiento. Her parents educated her in manual arts and basic literacy. She worked as a seamstress and embroiderer. She married Marco Gómez on 8 No
2 CONC vember 1833. She was a member of the Sociedad de Beneficencia. She died in San Juan on 14 March 1899. (Sosa de Newton, 587)
2 CONT
2 CONT Life Events
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1803 She was born in San Juan on 1 April 1803. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1833 She married Marco Gómez on 8 November 1833. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1899 She died in San Juan on 14 March 1899. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Sosa de Newton, Lily, (1986), Diccionario biográfico de mujeres argentinas
